// Every constant here was **read out of `sauria_targets.h`** in the verified,
// patched source tree, not transcribed. That distinction is the whole point:
// the geometry is a C++ template parameter whose defaults are 32x32 for
// `NpuTop` and 32x64 for `SystolicArray`, and INT8 requires no `-D` at all, so
// an adapter that omits its template arguments compiles cleanly and runs a
// different array. A table copied into this repository would be a second truth
// that drifts; these values cannot disagree with the source they came from
// because they *are* the source's values.
//
// `sauria_geometry.h` turns them into `static_assert`s against the
// template arguments the adapter actually instantiates, which is what closes
// the gap between "the source says 64x64" and "we compiled 64x64".

